metadata.solution:
Begin by distributing in the innermost parentheses: \begin{align*}
&\ \ \ \ x\left(x(1+x)+2x\right)-3(x^2-x+2) \\&= x(x+x^2+2x) - 3(x^2-x+2)
\end{align*} Now, distribute again: \begin{align*}
x^2+x^3+2x^2-3x^2+3x-6
\end{align*} Finally, combine like terms to get \begin{align*}
\boxed{x^3+3x-6}
\end{align*}

The area of the parallelogram generated by $\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}$ is given by
\[\|\overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB}\| = \left\| \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = \left\| \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -10 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \right\| = 6 \sqrt{5}.\][asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

A = (0,0);
B = (7,2);
C = (1,3);
D = B + C;

draw(A--B,Arrow(6));
draw(A--C,Arrow(6));
draw(B--C);
draw(B--D--C,dashed);

label("$O$", A, SW);
label("$A$", B, SE);
label("$B$", C, W);
[/asy]

Therefore, the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\boxed{3 \sqrt{5}}.$

A $y$-intercept is a point on the graph that lies on the $y$-axis, so $x = 0$.  Hence, the number $y$-intercepts corresponds to the number of real solutions of the quadratic equation $y^2 - 4y - 1 = 0$.  The discriminant of this quadratic equation is $(-4)^2 + 4 \cdot 1 \cdot (-1) = 20$, which is positive, so the quadratic has two distinct real roots.  Therefore, the number of $y$-intercepts is $\boxed{2}$.

